                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "be2227ad-97e2-3865-a650-60fcbb998ed7",
                        "entry_id": "18689b13-e794-3d7d-ba2c-c38100e6c52d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif aux matrices."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdc14371-b14b-4449-a9b1-ef49c8fa76fb",
                                "sense_id": "be2227ad-97e2-3865-a650-60fcbb998ed7",
                                "text": "Et je me disais que, même transcrit en calcul matriciel avec la constante h réformant la notion de déterminisme et la constante c pour la refonte des concepts d’espace et de temps, l’absurde de l’homme ne se résoudrait jamais […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d61b693e-07c4-35f8-9bef-26d68f4cc7f5",
                        "entry_id": "18689b13-e794-3d7d-ba2c-c38100e6c52d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif aux matrices cadastrales."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcbd4cd2-e0aa-4b99-8d71-1707f9ed9b1d",
                                "sense_id": "d61b693e-07c4-35f8-9bef-26d68f4cc7f5",
                                "text": "Voici mon amendement dans sa nouvelle rédaction : « A partir du 1ᵉʳ janvier 1850, le contingent des contributions des portes et fenêtres attribué à chaque commune sera réuni à la contribution foncière assise sur les propriétés bâties. Cette réunion s'opérera en élevant le revenu matriciel desdites propriétés dans la proportion nécessaire pour absorber le contingent des contributions des portes et fenêtres attribué à la commune. »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04eca91e-56da-48d6-a3c9-64d85a39d4cb",
                        "source_entry_id": "18689b13-e794-3d7d-ba2c-c38100e6c52d",
                        "target_lang_word": "matrix",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "matrix",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75cfaa47-08cd-3e85-910b-416bd54c38e1",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The cavity or mold in which anything is formed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93ee0f1e-f45c-37f7-9f88-eae159346602",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The womb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee755502-3aae-4590-a251-30b6778beee5",
                                                "sense_id": "93ee0f1e-f45c-37f7-9f88-eae159346602",
                                                "text": "upon conception the inward orifice of the matrix exactly closeth, so that it commonly admitteth nothing after […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f21af16c-b02d-40bc-a851-34dc3c060dd1",
                                                "sense_id": "93ee0f1e-f45c-37f7-9f88-eae159346602",
                                                "text": "In very rare cases, when the matrix just goes on pegging away automatically, the doctor can take advantage of that and ease out the second brat who then can be considered to be, say, three minutes younger […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ea34936-3567-3f1a-9c07-29c00446899c",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The metaphorical place where something is made, formed, or given birth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "869d23b0-8343-4942-a2da-bf3deb025ce3",
                                                "sense_id": "3ea34936-3567-3f1a-9c07-29c00446899c",
                                                "text": "When it is remembered that ritual dancing was the matrix out of which the Drama sprang, and further that the drama in its inception (as still to-day in India) was an affair of religion and was acted in, or in connection with, the Temples, it becomes easier to understand how all this mass of ceremonial sacrifices, expiations, initiations, Sun and Nature festivals, eucharistic and orgiastic communions and celebrations, mystery-plays, dramatic representations, myths and legends, etc. [...] have practically sprung from the same root: a root deep and necessary in the psychology of Man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ceed305-ebae-3f34-95de-8ea5beeed141",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The material or tissue in which more specialized structures are embedded."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88edb993-7b03-3ea6-b260-6f0c114eab12",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extracellular matrix, the material or tissue between the cells of animals or plants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46395380-2c85-3dfe-9a46-ede400cf47d3",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Part of the mitochondrion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5faaa71d-0f33-3702-bc09-d20f857f30c9",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The medium in which bacteria are cultured."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ae3410c-5d94-3791-98d8-ba049b6d7d42",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A table of data."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd256734-3276-34ae-bf0f-68774503a6bf",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rectangular arrangement of numbers or terms having various uses such as transforming coordinates in geometry, solving systems of linear equations in linear algebra and representing graphs in graph theory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4674ae9-8f02-4b0c-bddb-a10378a25442",
                                                "sense_id": "bd256734-3276-34ae-bf0f-68774503a6bf",
                                                "text": "Theorem (7.5.2) then says that every positive semidefinite matrix is a convex combination of matrices that lie on extreme rays."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7240938-ae05-4b00-a40a-6b26c50c0fae",
                                                "sense_id": "bd256734-3276-34ae-bf0f-68774503a6bf",
                                                "text": "Check that the #92;mathcal#123;A#125;(#92;mathcal#123;D#125;)² in the example is itself the adjacency matrix of the indicated digraph:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7015f7aa-6419-45c5-baa4-3f7656086c1f",
                                                "sense_id": "bd256734-3276-34ae-bf0f-68774503a6bf",
                                                "text": "2007, Gerhard Kloos, Matrix Methods for Optical Layout, SPIE Press, page 25,\nThe matrix describing the reflection at a plane mirror can be obtained by taking the matrix for reflection at a spherical reflector and letting the radius of the spherical mirror tend to infinity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44981e71-b0d2-4d5f-9ae1-90ba6fd29c1d",
                                                "sense_id": "bd256734-3276-34ae-bf0f-68774503a6bf",
                                                "text": "The Fibonacci numbers have been widely studied, and the different ways to generate those numbers have gained continued interest, among them matrix methods [10], determinants [5], permanents [6], Pascal’s triangle [9], binomial coefficients [3], and many others [8]. […] In [1] two tridiagonal Toeplitz matrices were presented […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ee3cec7-2ab6-3a92-89b4-c58cbbd3a267",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A two-dimensional array."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e308545-7d97-32ed-b6fc-3e3f4beae809",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Matrix; a controlled environment or situation in which people behave in ways that conform to pre-determined roles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ddac239-5f22-402a-a988-14481e33d46c",
                                                "sense_id": "4e308545-7d97-32ed-b6fc-3e3f4beae809",
                                                "text": "He'd operated on an almost permanent adrenaline high, a byproduct of youth and proficiency, jacked into a custom cyberspace deck that projected his disembodied consciousness into the consensual hallucination that was the matrix."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a7c19b0-f457-47cc-9583-f9b24e5dd314",
                                                "sense_id": "4e308545-7d97-32ed-b6fc-3e3f4beae809",
                                                "text": "Mari Otsu, a 25-year-old Japanese-Hawaiian artist, tells me she was “desperately lonely” while she was studying at New York University, when she “realised that [she]^([sic]) was in the matrix”. I ask her what she means."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53748031-b8b8-343a-9195-c30721b775c6",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A grid-like arrangement of electronic components, especially one intended for information coding, decoding or storage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad311139-3972-447b-8c0d-4aa3761a8214",
                                                "sense_id": "53748031-b8b8-343a-9195-c30721b775c6",
                                                "text": "Any type of core or diode matrix used to derive the decoding of these codes would amount to a rather large volume of terminals for just the 17,500 terminals alone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd6927a8-cf88-48ae-8de2-fd64f20a5ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "53748031-b8b8-343a-9195-c30721b775c6",
                                                "text": "The transistor matrix in the encoder supplies the sequential gates."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2248298c-7df4-4183-b5d0-9b342f70d2fd",
                                                "sense_id": "53748031-b8b8-343a-9195-c30721b775c6",
                                                "text": "A transistor-diode matrix is composed of vertical and horizontal wires with a transistor at each intersection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03bead51-3ca1-49ea-b010-d7a38f5a61e2",
                                                "sense_id": "53748031-b8b8-343a-9195-c30721b775c6",
                                                "text": "Robot controllers range in complexity from simple stepping switches through pneumatic logic sequencers, diode matrix boards, electronic sequencers, and microprocessors to minicomputers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cb41fce-6b6f-4025-80c5-3de64a059dcc",
                                                "sense_id": "53748031-b8b8-343a-9195-c30721b775c6",
                                                "text": "Diode matrix is the most fundamental of all ROM structure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe77d6cc-ce2b-378e-b007-3c8ca9543b3f",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A geological matrix."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "423c29cb-5f25-3cca-8ddf-dd82ccde9bb6",
                                        "entry_id": "eec27d3d-eb72-36b6-aea0-4f8d7a105bfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The sediment surrounding and including the artifacts, features, and other materials at a site."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
